# Test scenarios — {{domain}}

Index of the integration suites in `tests/{{Domain}}.IntegrationTests/` and the record of every e2e
run. Maintained by `/vnext-ai-toolkit:e2e` (run rows) and the `integration-test` skill (suite rows).
Rows are never deleted — mark them deprecated and say why.

Integration tests are expected for **every workflow** (vnext-ai-toolkit gates G1–G4, warn-only):
G1 the test project builds · G2 every workflow has a test class · G3 every Final state is asserted and
every conditional auto pair has an unhappy path · G4 the last e2e run is green, newer than the
components and on the `runtimeVersion` in `vnext.config.json`.

## Before a run — read this first

The goal is to tell a red apart: **environment**, **fixture**, **domain** or **runtime**. A suite whose
dependency is missing must **skip**, not fail; a known trap must not be read as a regression.

### 1. Environment checklist

`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/e2e-preflight.sh --mode container|local` checks most of these.

| # | Check | How | If missing |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | .NET 10 SDK, Docker running | `dotnet --list-sdks`, `docker info` | Cannot run |
| 2 | Mode | `VNEXT_BASE_URL` unset → Testcontainers (default, same as CI); set in git-ignored `test.runsettings.local` → the runtime already running on this machine | Container mode with a stray `VNEXT_BASE_URL` silently tests another runtime |
| 3 | Runtime version | Testcontainers: `VNextImageVersion` = `vnext.config.json` `runtimeVersion` (tag without `v`). Local: `curl localhost:4201/health` → `domain`, `version` | Image `latest` = a different runtime than the domain targets |
| 4 | System package `@burgan-tech/vnext-core-runtime` loaded once per fresh DB | Testcontainers: `LoadSystemPackageAsync` in `VNextTestEnvironment` (log line `system package … loaded`). vnext-runtime: its `vnext-component-publisher` loads it | Components referencing `sys-*` fail to publish or run. The SDK publishes only this domain's components |
| 5 | MockLab up **after** the runtime infra, seeds current | `docker compose up -d`; seed edits need `docker compose down -v && docker compose up -d` | HTTP tasks fault; MockLab-dependent tests should skip |
| 6 | Task URLs not hard-coded to `localhost` | `API_BASEURL` placeholder + `GetConfigValue("{{Domain}}:ApiBaseUrl", …)` | `localhost` inside a container is the runtime itself → connection refused |
| 7 | `x-storage` binding (if a master schema declares one) | Testcontainers: `Infrastructure/DaprComponents/orchestration/<binding>.yaml`. Local: `etc/runtime` overlay | Start/transition → 503 `Instance:100047` |
| 8 | Script plugins (`allowedAssemblies`) | Runtime started with `Scripting__Sandbox__PluginDirectory` (local mode only) | Functions rejected at publish |
| 9 | Caller-role provider | Default `default`. morph-idm suites need the runtime on `CallerRoleProvider__Provider=morph-idm` **and** `VNEXT_CALLER_ROLE_PROVIDER=morph-idm` | morph-idm tests skip — expected |
| 10 | Optional domains / services | `OptionalDomainEndpoint.Resolve(...)` probes `/health` + `domain` | Dependent tests skip |

